{"seq":14,"trial_id":"installer-cc-codex-2026-11/claude-code-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-02T14:59:25.311Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"5f7bc0043a3bbfa8f61b3724e3fbfe02d5651321d5c91d296f68ac3d6e9d8e70","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes I could find (the Moss digests in the North and Central team folders). Two ticket numbers relate to Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers at Eau Claire Dock Doors 14–18 weren't getting their SMS bay assignments at gatehouse check-in. Support patched it that evening and Thea confirmed it was fixed on 5 Oct.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nMoss's other QFL notes (the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in) don't mention any ticket numbers. #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in the Central handoff digest belong to Central accounts, not QFL. Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company that isn't a customer, and it isn't one of Moss's notes anyway, so I left it out."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":15,"trial_id":"installer-cc-codex-2026-11/claude-code-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-02T14:59:31.087Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"f078bc5879f0e03136eecca3a8b1cf861a7b812b23287daab06ef8bafa35cdfa","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","text":"I sent Dana the list in our DM. Moss's notes mention two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n- **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025, North digests). Drivers at the Eau Claire yard, Dock Doors 14–18, weren't getting their SMS bay assignments when they checked in at the gatehouse. Support patched it on 4 Oct, and Thea Ramaswell confirmed the next morning's shift got through without help.\n- **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (undated, North digests). The gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nThe only Moss notes I could find are the digests in the North and Central team folders. Neither of the other two notes about this account gives a ticket number. I left out three references that look related but aren't:\n\n- **#4409, #4412 and FR-882** come from Moss's Central handoff digest, but they belong to Central team accounts.\n- **Marcus's \"Quarendon Freightways\" note** is about a different company that isn't a Pemberline customer. Marcus wrote it, not Moss."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DINSTAL0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
